## Author request

Find a clearer word than "Commission" for the harness memory department
holding the author's intent and pinned rulings, then migrate the name.
The current label is ambiguous; this is a naming and reference migration,
not a redesign of memory or the authority/promotion workflow.

## Scope

Compare plain-language names against the page's actual purpose, choose one,
and explain the choice briefly. Migrate the current topic filename/heading,
index entry, and active harness instructions and links naming this department
as one coherent change. Search the full logical unit rather than applying a
blind replacement to unrelated uses of "commission".

Relevant starting points:
- `memory/topics/user-rulings.md` (renamed from `commission.md`)
- `memory/MEMORY.md`
- `skills/smelt/references/consolidation.md`
- Other active references found by the migration audit.

The seventh-smelt proposal is currently PR2263; coordinate with its outcome
and the author's manual edits before migrating. Do not overwrite those edits.
Other projects' memory files are outside this ticket's write scope.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A clearer name is selected and justified by the page's role: author
  intent and rulings, rather than an institutional metaphor.
- [ ] The topic filename, heading, index, and all active harness references
  are migrated consistently; active links resolve.
- [ ] Pinned quotations and their meaning remain intact. Journal entries,
  accepted reports and historical ledgers are not rewritten; retained legacy
  references are identified and their handling explained.
- [ ] The migration changes no authority, rule-promotion process, or memory
  guarantees. Applicable memory caps remain respected, with any existing
  pinned-content overflow explicitly preserved and reported.
- [ ] The final diff and reference/link checks demonstrate a complete active
  migration without renaming unrelated uses of the word.
